  "result": "Perfect! All 96 tests pass. I've successfully added line discount support to the invoicing system:\n\n**src/errors.js** - Added error code:\n- `DISCOUNT_INVALID`: For discounts outside 0-100 or non-numeric values\n\n**src/invoices.js** - Added discount functionality:\n\n1. **lineDiscount(line)** - Calculates discount for a line:\n   - Formula: `lineTotal * discountPercent / 100`\n   - Rounds result using `roundCents()` to ensure whole cents\n   - Defaults to 0 if discountPercent is undefined\n\n2. **Updated createInvoice**:\n   - Accepts optional `discountPercent` in line input\n   - Validates it's a number from 0-100 (can be decimal like 12.5)\n   - Returns `DISCOUNT_INVALID` for invalid values\n   - Stores on each line, defaulting to 0\n\n3. **Updated invoiceTotals**:\n   - Now returns `{ subtotal, discount, total }`\n   - `subtotal`: sum of all lineTotal amounts\n   - `discount`: sum of all lineDiscount amounts\n   - `total`: subtotal - discount, clamped at 0\n\n4. **Updated addLine**:\n   - Accepts optional `discountPercent` parameter\n   - Validates same as createInvoice\n   - Stores on new lines, defaulting to 0\n\n**Tests** - 20 new tests covering:\n- Discount storage and defaults\n- Validation for out-of-range and non-numeric values\n- Decimal discount support\n- Correct discount calculations\n- Multiple line discount summation\n- Total clamping at zero",
